  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Determine the Ramsey number $ R(C_4,S_n), $ where $S_n=K_{1,n}$ is the star on $n+1$ vertices.\nIn particular, is it true that, for any $c>0$, there are infinitely many $n$ such that $ R(C_4,S_n)\\leq n+\\sqrt{n}-c? $ ",
